## SEVERITY / VERDICT (decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker (a STOP for Tuesday):* a path beyond the three; any byte of `main.bicep`, `env/*`, `scripts/*`, `.github/**`, `api/**`, `web/**`; the switch or a key compiling ON in dev; **a demo or uat key naming another environment's secret or vault, a literal or typed host, or empty with the switch on**; any uat cell different from main's; the demo arm NOT on main (the template would turn on a switch the code refuses, or an unguarded one); a code path that opens outside uat and the demo's own sites; a secret VALUE, a person's name, a decision-card id or a `B###`/ticket key in an added line or the message; non-ASCII in an added line; a skip/sleep/retry/environment gate added to a test; the head moved; a textual conflict; a CodeQL alert open on the head; a failing required check; a merge that would deploy the template; an existing assertion loosened, deleted or made conditional with no restatement (C1 mapping broken).
*Major, class SAME:* any setting of either site, in any environment, changing besides the demo's four (class d); a guard row green against main's template while titled for the demo cell, or red for another reason than its title (class f); a mutant of G1-G9 or G12 that survives (a Blocker if it lets a switch on in dev or a wrong secret/vault through; Major otherwise); the in-test reader returning a value that differs from your evaluator (class f); a claim in the PR title, body, commit or a row title that no run carries and that hides a defect.
*Major, class DIFFERENT:* a builder claim contradicted by measurement with a verdict consequence (277 / 267; 156 cells / 4 changed; 10 red-first rows; 8 of 8; 8 leaves).
*Minor / Note (never a Major):* the commit message's 96 / 86 against 99 / 89 (Minor: wording, Tuesday words the squash message); `infra/env/uat.bicepparam:3` and the two refusal texts naming `uat-open-key` (log text, outside the paths: follow-up ticket text); G13 if shown equivalent; the demo site-name suffix equality (UNMEASURED; mismatch fails closed); the unsigned commit; the 3.9 `test_resource_hygiene` failure reproduced at main; the `mkdtemp` leak of the suite; the raw ARM text of the four settings changing in every environment (one `main.json`); README touching two sentences where the stamp allowed one (disclosed; true).
*Where the line between Note and Major is unclear:* a thing that lets a switch open where it must not, names another environment's secret, hides a change, or makes a guard row unable to fail is at least Major SAME; a thing that only narrows a row, stays true to the commission and is disclosed, is a Note. Say which rule you applied for every finding. A security-shaped finding is a STOP for Tuesday.
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs every check clean and measured, the C2 table complete (dev, uat equal, demo exact, 4 of 156 changed), the C3 demo arm read at the head, C4 mutants killed (G13 aside), 0 findings above Note, CodeQL (every language) and the five required contexts `success` on the CURRENT head (a not-finished or NOT STARTED row caps at GO WITH FINDINGS (conditional) with the condition named). GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note/Condition only. NO GO on any Blocker or Major (round 1 of 2: FOR TUESDAY then carries the CLOSED list with cells, the RESIDUE as ticket text with the tester's cells attached, and the fix shape in prose: one new commit on the same branch, forward only). NOT GATED = the head moved or a guarded path moved on main.
